🚨 **BLOCKING — fixed**

The stale `#515` assertion is updated to the gh-2096 semantics — the fix is exactly the one requested: assert the **per-call child token** was cancelled and the **run-wide budget token stayed live**.

Commit: `ad1c56dfa1` (+ the interleaved WIP auto-save `51698433bb`; net rework diff vs `d57ee076`: 1 file, +20/−4) on `ai/gh-2096` (`test/agent/auto_compactor_structured_budget_test.dart`, the `structured engine, direct: the hide judge budget kill` test):

```dart
// gh-2096: the engine hands every judge call a per-call child token
// — capture it to assert the abort reached the provider layer.
final judgeTokens = <CancelToken>[];
...
judge: (ledger, [token]) {
  if (token != null) judgeTokens.add(token);
  return Completer<String?>().future;
},
...
expect(judgeTokens, hasLength(2));
expect(judgeTokens.every((t) => t.isCancelled), isTrue);
expect(
  budgetSource.token.isCancelled,
  isFalse,
  reason: 'a judge timeout must not cancel the run-wide budget token',
);
```

Notes on the shape of the fix:

- `hasLength(2)` (not 1) is deliberate and matches this PR's own semantics: after the first per-call timeout the retry stays live, so the engine fires **both** judge attempts — each under its own child token, each killed by its own budget expiry (#515 preserved at the provider layer via the forwarded child tokens). This mirrors `structured_judge_health_test.dart` (`receivedTokens, hasLength(2)` / `liveAtReceive` / `every((t) => t.isCancelled)`), so the two tests now encode the same behavior instead of contradictory behavior.
- `budgetSource.token.isCancelled` is now asserted **false** — the engine code is untouched (as the finding states, only the stale assertion needed the update).
- The test no longer relies on the old mechanism: it now fails if the engine ever cancels the run-wide token on a judge timeout, which is exactly the regression gh-2096 fixed (the "born-cancelled retry").

Verification on the branch:

- `dart test test/agent/auto_compactor_structured_budget_test.dart --plain-name "the hide judge budget kill"` → **1 passed** (was the reported `Expected: true / Actual: <false>` at `351:5`).
- `dart test test/agent/auto_compactor_structured_budget_test.dart` → **7 passed**.
- `dart test test/compaction/structured_judge_health_test.dart test/compaction/structured_judge_fallback_test.dart test/compaction/structured_engine_test.dart` (the PR's verify commands) → **31 passed**.
- Full `test/compaction + test/agent` sweep → green (no regressions; this was the only failing test in the CI Core/Hostile runs).
